WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.424
In the traditional story, Bi Gan was a loyal minister of the late Shang.

00:00:05.774 --> 00:00:09.590
He was an upright man, and everyone respected him greatly.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.924
But King Zhou's behavior grew more and more unreasonable.

00:00:14.274 --> 00:00:18.306
The other ministers dared not speak, but Bi Gan was deeply worried.

00:00:18.656 --> 00:00:23.600
Bi Gan gathered his courage and offered his advice to King Zhou.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:28.558
He hoped the king would change his ways and govern the country well.

00:00:28.908 --> 00:00:32.676
Legend says King Zhou was furious and refused to listen to him.

00:00:33.026 --> 00:00:36.890
The utterly loyal Bi Gan in the end lost his life.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.888
Later generations deeply admired Bi Gan and often honor his memory.

00:00:41.238 --> 00:00:45.798
People use his story to praise the courage of speaking the truth.

00:00:46.148 --> 00:00:50.540
This tragic episode mainly comes from later writings.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:55.018
We cannot treat it entirely as verified history.

